            "review_title": "Review at Spice Temple - Estella",
            "review_text": "Gin128\n17 contributions\n1\nGood experience at Spice Temple\nDec 2018 • Friends\nHad lunch with my partner. The restaurant has another branch in downtown (81 Mac Thi Buoi street, District 1), but this one is new version. Located 2nd floor of Estella Place. It took me 10 minutes to get here from downtown.\nWe started off with Grill Pork Satay and Prawn cakes. Both were delicious. Steam sea bass with green chili sauce was really spicy, but I loved it. Olive fried rice with minced chicken was great.\nGood service.\nFor a restaurant in mall, I wanna say the price is affordable. I highly recommend this restaurant to everyone who loves Thai food. Will comeback soon!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 7, 2019\nLeKienLki\nGood morning Gin,\nWe are extremely delighted to know how satisfied you are. It makes us really glad to read your compliments about our delicious dishes.\nThank you for sharing your experience you had with Spice Temple Estella.\nHopefully, you keep supporting us by coming back next time.\n\nHave a good day!\nRead more\nWritten January 18, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
